# Fleet development overlay — local only, never published.
.mcp.json
.willow/
.cursor/

# The trust root. CLAUDE.md refusal 2: contract and policy are versioned,
# grants are not. Neither path is in this tree today, and until 2026-07-31
# nothing kept them out either — see docs/SECURITY-AUDIT.md TM-ROOT-01. This
# is the mitigation; the enforcement half is `.githooks/pre-commit` (installed
# by `scripts/install-hooks.sh`), which reads the staged set and refuses a
# force-add `.gitignore` cannot catch. Written 2026-07-31, TM-ROOT-01.
mcp_apps/
_net_leases/
*.grant
*.lease
# tests/ablate.py's lock and recovery sidecar.
.ablate-lock
.ablate-inflight.json
# tests/ablate_store.py's, which are separate files under separate names. The
# two lines above were written for the one harness that existed at the time and
# the store registry arrived later with its own; until this line the store
# sidecar showed up as an *untracked* file mid-run, so `git add -A` swept it in.
# It carries a full copy of the unmutated target as a JSON string — a 30 KB
# `migrations/003_row_security.sql` was the observed case — so committing it
# publishes the recovery record for a mutation still in flight, beside the
# mutated file itself. A glob rather than two names, so a third registry does
# not repeat this (§16 rule 5: the middle is the thing that rots).
.ablate-*

# Agent-session working copies — harness state, never project content.
.claude/worktrees/
